{
  "id": "fa_practical",
  "title": "Persian — practical English romanization (Iranian style)",
  "language": "fa",
  "script": "Arab",
  "kind": "practical",
  "status": "informal",
  "ascii": true,
  "authority": "Common Iranian passport and press practice ('BGN/PCGN without diacritics, with Persian vowels'); not a formal standard",
  "description": "Readable ASCII spellings as Iranians write their names in English: short vowels a e o (Mohammad, Hossein, Reza), ū = ou (Mahmoud, Masoud), ey = ei (Hossein, Zeinab), gh for both غ and ق (Ghasem), v for و, kh sh zh ch, final silent h = -eh (Fatemeh, Zadeh), Allāh compounds joined with -ollah (Abdollah, Nasrollah), Abd + article = Abdol (Abdolreza). Known names come from the lexicon (latin['fa']).",
  "sources": [
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanization_of_Persian",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persian_name",
    "https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e1eeaafe5274a4f0f57553a/ROMANIZATION_OF_PERSIAN.pdf",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hussein"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Lexicon spellings win (Mehdi, Reza, Hossein); the rules only handle vocalised input and names the lexicon does not know. No template vocalisation is applied to Persian.",
    "s between two short vowels is doubled (Hossein, Hassan, Hessam), but not after a word-initial vowel (Asad).",
    "ZWNJ (U+200C) is removed and surname parts are joined (Ahmadinejad, Kazemzadeh).",
    "The Arabic article inside compound names is joined with o (Nouroddin, Zeinolabedin); Abd + article is Abdol (Abdolrahman); names ending in Allah take -ollah.",
    "ʿayn is dropped, except that a + ʿayn before a consonant gives aa (Saadi); hamza is dropped."
  ],
  "alphabet": "ءآأؤئابپتثجچحخدذرزژسشصضطظعغفقکگلمنوهیةۀ",
  "hook": "arabic",
